    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Born of the 1868 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> went from feudal isolation to industrial great power in barely a generation.</li><li>Its 1905 defeat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> showed the colonised world that European supremacy was not inevitable.</li><li>A system with no check on its military drove it into a war it could not sustain, ending in surrender in 1945.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> imported roughly 80 per cent of its oil from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, so the American <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/us-oil-embargo-against-japan">oil embargo</a> of August 1941 pushed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-tokyo">Tokyo</a> towards attacking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

