l <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/togo">Togo</a> annihilates the Russian fleet at Tsushima, sealing victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1931</span><span class="rf-text">Army officers stage the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukden-incident">Mukden Incident</a>, launching independent action in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1941</span><span class="rf-text">US <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/us-oil-embargo-against-japan">oil embargo</a> in August pushes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> towards the attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1942</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> loses four <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aircraft-carrier">fleet carriers</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway">Midway</a>, surrendering the strategic initiative</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1945</span><span class="rf-text">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a> and Soviet entry into the war, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> surrenders aboard <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uss-missouri">USS Missouri</a></span></li></ol>
